====Quirks====
A restriction that causes a Pokémon's catch factor to be a minimum of 3 after bait has been thrown, causes {{p|Chansey}}'s [[catch rate]] to be increased from 25 (4.9% per Safari Ball) to 38 (8.09% per Safari Ball) after throwing bait. This means that throwing bait makes Chansey both easier to catch and less likely to flee. Similarly {{p|Kangaskhan}}, {{p|Scyther}}, {{p|Pinsir}}, {{p|Tauros}}, {{p|Dratini}}, and {{p|Dragonair}} all have catch rates that are unaffected by the use of bait. Due to this oddity, using bait and throwing Safari Balls in specific sequences allows the player to optimize their odds of catching the rare Pokémon. 

However, as Pokémon's flee check is performed at the beginning of the turn, this means bait and rock will only come into effect the turn after it has been thrown. This leaves an inherent risk of a Pokémon fleeing before any Safari Ball has been thrown if the player chooses to use bait on first turn; conversely, if the player has only one Safari Ball, the penalty for throwing rock the turn before using it will be effectively ignored due to the player's Safari Game ending on the turn it would come into the effect. 

Additionally, in Japanese versions of the games, bait and rock do not work correctly and only affect the catch factor, meaning that outside of the above mentioned species, bait actually hinders player's odds of catching the Pokémon, while rocks increase them with no downsides.

